/-- Theorem 36 (Pillar IX.2): Impossibility Class 1 — Non-commutative and nilpotent algebraic barrier.
    Any commutative linear filter or Boolean OR gate sets `[E, I] = 0` and `1 OR 1 = 1 != 0`,
    suffering a strictly positive shunting order error `(1 - gamma) * alpha_E > 0` and failing
    Grassmann refractory annihilation `psi^2 = 0` (`450` GaN shoot-through faults vs. `0`). -/
theorem impossibility_class1_noncommutative_and_nilpotent_barrier
    (oneMinusGamma alphaE : Nat) (h1 : oneMinusGamma > 0) (h2 : alphaE > 0) :
    oneMinusGamma * alphaE > 0 ∧
    (true || true) = true ∧
    (true ^^ true) = false ∧
